 "text": "Lia Fáil is an Irish stone of legend. It is one of four great magic tools of the Tuatha Dé Danann, the folk of the goddess Danu. This stone pillar screamed when the true king touched it. It came from the Otherworld, from the magic city of Fálias. The other tools were a spear that never missed, a sword none could stop, and a cauldron that never ran dry. The stone stood on the hill of Tara for the crowning of the High King. A stone still stands on the hill. Some say the true stone never left the Otherworld. Others hold it crossed the sea to Scotland.",
